# README i18n format

When creating or editing project `README.md` files, use this structure.

## Required layout

1. Sections in order: `## English` → `## 日本語` → `## 中文(简体)`
2. Separate languages with a `---` line
3. Put the topic title under each language as `### …`
4. Prefer `#### Related documentation` / `#### 関連ドキュメント` / `#### 相关文档` for doc links

## Link rules

- English docs: `documents/<name>.md`
- Japanese: `documents/i18n/ja/<name>.md`
- Chinese: `documents/i18n/zh-CN/<name>.md`
- Links to other `README.md` files keep the same path in all languages
- Keep code, paths, type names, and define symbols unchanged; translate prose only
- Link only to **user-facing** docs under `Assets/MIDI/documents/`. Never link READMEs to `.cursor/plans/` or `docs/dev/` (see `dev-plans-vs-release-docs.mdc`)

## Example skeleton

```markdown
## English

### Topic Title

Brief description.

#### Related documentation

- [Samples](../../documents/samples.md)

---

## 日本語

### トピックタイトル

簡単な説明。

#### 関連ドキュメント

- [サンプル](../../documents/i18n/ja/samples.md)

---

## 中文(简体)

### 主题标题

简要说明。

#### 相关文档

- [示例](../../documents/i18n/zh-CN/samples.md)
```

## Exceptions

Do not rewrite upstream vendor package root READMEs under trees such as `UdpMidi2Discovery/*/` package roots or `RTP-MIDI-for-.NET/` package roots unless explicitly asked. Project-owned directory READMEs under `Assets/MIDI/` and the repo root must follow this format.

## Not covered by this rule

- `docs/dev/**` and `.cursor/plans/**` are internal. Do not apply `documents/i18n/` layout to them, and do not “fill gaps” by copying plans/spikes into `Assets/MIDI/documents/`.
- Optional translations for internal archives (if any) belong under `docs/dev/i18n/` only.
